1
00:00:00,830 --> 00:00:02,280
See.

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:08,090
Simon is talking about the weather with his grandpa in Harbin on the phone.

3
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:13,040
Work in pairs and talk about the weather in your area.

4
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:20,040
Use the conversation below as a model. Hello, grandpa.

5
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:22,060
This is Simon.

6
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:26,480
How are you doing? Hi, Simon.

7
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:30,610
I'm fine, but it's really cold.

8
00:00:30,610 --> 00:00:36,480
There was a heavy snowstorm here in Harbin yesterday.

9
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:45,150
It's difficult to get around the city with so much snow. Oh dear!

10
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:48,140
The weather is so awful.

11
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:51,300
You'd better not go out.

12
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:58,360
I can order things for you online, grandpa. Thanks, Simon.

13
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:00,410
I can manage.

14
00:01:00,410 --> 00:01:06,110
I hope the snow will melt soon. OK.

15
00:01:06,110 --> 00:01:10,520
Feel free to call us if you need help.

16
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:14,660
Take care, grandpa. Bye-bye.

17
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:18,230
You take care too. Bye.
